              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Latin for a young person, then the Latin for a widow."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: rēgula, rēgulae",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "rēgula, rēgulae — \"a rule, a ruler\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "rēgula is built on regō, \"to keep straight, to rule\" (Lewis & Short), with -ula, an ending for a tool: a straight stick, a ruler. English rule comes from it through French."
            }
          ]
        },
